@startuml proximadb-data-flow
!theme plain
title ProximaDB Data Flow - Sequence Diagram

participant "REST Client" as RC
participant "REST Handler" as RH
participant "SharedServices" as SS
participant "VectorService" as VS
participant "CollectionService" as CS
participant "WAL Manager" as WM
participant "Storage Engine" as SE
participant "Metadata Backend" as MB

== Collection Creation Flow ==
RC -> RH: POST /api/v1/collection\n{operation: "create", config: {...}}
activate RH
RH -> RH: convert_to_proto_config()
note right: DUPLICATE: Conversion logic
RH -> SS: get collection_service()
SS --> RH: Arc<CollectionService>
RH -> CS: create_collection(proto_config)
activate CS
CS -> MB: create_collection(proto_config)
MB --> CS: proto::Collection
CS -> SS: assignment_service.assign()
CS --> RH: CreateCollectionResponse
deactivate CS
RH -> RH: convert_from_proto_collection()
note right: DUPLICATE: Conversion logic
RH --> RC: JSON Response
deactivate RH

== Vector Insertion Flow ==
RC -> RH: POST /api/v1/vector/batch\n{collection_id, vectors: [...]}
activate RH
RH -> RH: Convert JSON to VectorRecord
RH -> RH: create_avro_vector_batch()
note right: LEGACY: Should use Proto
RH -> SS: get vector_service()
SS --> RH: Arc<VectorService>
RH -> VS: handle_vector_batch(collection_id, avro_payload)
activate VS
VS -> VS: validate_avro_payload()
note right: ERROR: Expects Avro but gets JSON
VS -> CS: get_collection(collection_id)
CS --> VS: Collection metadata
VS -> WM: write_vector_batch(batch)
activate WM
WM -> WM: strategy.serialize_batch()
note right: Uses Avro serialization
WM -> SE: insert_vector_batch()
SE --> WM: Success
WM --> VS: Sequence numbers
deactivate WM
VS --> RH: Success
deactivate VS
RH --> RC: JSON Response
deactivate RH

== Search Flow ==
RC -> RH: POST /api/v1/vector/search\n{collection_id, queries: [...]}
activate RH
RH -> VS: search_vectors_polymorphic()
activate VS
VS -> VS: Three-layer search:\n1. WAL\n2. Storage\n3. Compacted
VS -> CS: get_collection_config()
CS --> VS: Collection config
VS -> SE: search_vectors()
SE --> VS: Search results
VS --> RH: Vec<SearchResult>
deactivate VS
RH --> RC: JSON Response
deactivate RH

note over RH, VS
  KEY ISSUES:
  1. REST handler converts to Avro (legacy)
  2. Collection service is proto-first
  3. Duplicate conversion logic in handlers
  4. Vector service expects Avro not Proto
end note

@enduml